[{"title":"Nsenene","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene","category":"section","text":"Documentation for Nsenene.\n\n"},{"title":"Nsenene.densities","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene.densities-Tuple{Any, Any}","category":"method","text":"densities(profile, m)\n\nCalculate the mass density of each field in profile, with particle masses m.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"Nsenene.density","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene.density","category":"function","text":"density(profile, m)\n\nCalculate the total mass density of profile with particle masses m.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"Nsenene.gravitational_potential","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene.gravitational_potential","category":"function","text":"gravitational_potential(profile, m)\n\nCompute the gravitational potential due to the fields in profile with particle masses m.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"Nsenene.ground_state","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene.ground_state-NTuple{5, Any}","category":"method","text":"ground_state(m, Lambda, M, profile_type, resol; r_max=1.0)\n\nCalculate an approximate ground state for particle masses m, interactions Lambda and total masses M.\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"Nsenene.interaction_potential!","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene.interaction_potential!","category":"function","text":"interaction_potential!(V, profile, m, Lambda)\n\nAdd the interaction potential to the potential array V\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"Nsenene.kick!","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene.kick!-NTuple{4, Any}","category":"method","text":"kick(profile, h, m)\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"Nsenene.total_mass","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene.total_mass-Tuple{Any, Any}","category":"method","text":"total_mass(profile, m)\n\nCalculate the total mass contained in profile, with particle masses m. Returns a scalar.\n\nExamples\n\nimport Nsenene: CylindricalProfile, total_mass\n\nn = 2\nm = ones(1, 1, n)\n\np = CylindricalProfile(1000, 5.0, n)\n\n# psi 1 is a cylinder of density 1.0, radius 1.0, height 2.0\np.psi[:, :, 1] .= (p.R .< 1) .&& (abs.(p.z) .< 2.0/2)\n\nM = total_mass(p, m)\n@assert isapprox(M, 2pi, rtol=1e-2)\n\n# psi 2 is a cylinder of density 1.0, radius 1.0, height 4.0\np.psi[:, :, 2] .= (p.R .< 1) .&& (abs.(p.z) .< 4.0/2)\n\nM = total_mass(p, m)\n@assert isapprox(M, 2pi + 4pi, rtol=1e-2)\n\n0.0\n\n# output\n0.0\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"Nsenene.total_masses","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene.total_masses","category":"function","text":"total_masses(profile, m)\n\nCalculate the mass contained by each field in profile, with particle masses m. Returns an array of masses.\n\nExamples\n\nimport Nsenene: SphericalProfile, total_masses\n\nn = 3\nm = ones(1, n)\n\np = SphericalProfile(1000, 3.0, n)\n\n# Ball of radius 1\np.psi[:, 1] .= p.r .< 1\n# Ball of radius 2\np.psi[:, 2] .= p.r .< 2\n\nM = total_masses(p, m)\n\n@assert isapprox(M[1], 4/3 * π * 1^3, rtol=1e-2)\n@assert isapprox(M[2], 4/3 * π * 2^3, rtol=1e-2)\nM[3]\n\n# output\n\n0.0\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"Nsenene.Spherical._total_masses","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene.Spherical._total_masses-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","category":"method","text":"_total_masses(r, psi, m)\n\nCalculate the mass contained by each field of psi with radial coordinates r and particle masses m.\n\nExamples\n\nimport Nsenene.Spherical: _total_masses\n\nresol = 1000\nnfields = 2\n\nm = ones(1, nfields)\nr = range(0, 10, resol)\npsi = zeros(resol, nfields)\n\n# Ball of radius 1\npsi[r.<1, 1] .= 1\n\nM = _total_masses(psi, r, m)\n\n@assert isapprox(M[1], 4/3 * π * 1^3, atol=1e-1)\nM[2]\n\n# output\n\n0.0\n\n\n\n\n\n"},{"title":"Nsenene.Cylindrical.CylindricalProfile","page":"Home","location":"#Nsenene.Cylindrical.CylindricalProfile","category":"type","text":"struct CylindricalProfile\n\nExamples\n\nimport Nsenene.Cylindrical: CylindricalProfile\n\nresol_R = 64\nresol_z = 128\n\nlength_R = 10.0\nlength_z = 20.0\n\nnfields = 2\n\np = CylindricalProfile(resol_R, resol_z, length_R, length_z, nfields)\nmaximum(p.R)\n\n# output\n\n10.0\n\n\n\n\n\n"}]
